This directory holds the original XQuest v1.3 game data files.

These ARE checked into git. Mark Mackey's original license (see
LICENSE.DOC in the original distribution, quoted in this repo's LICENSE)
explicitly permits free redistribution:

    "You are free to upload this software to an electronic bulletin
    board (BBS), ftp site or other network and to make copies to give
    to your friends, so long as all of the files in the original
    distribution of XQuest are distributed together."

This repo bundles the game DATA (not the original Pascal source/binary,
which this port doesn't need or redistribute) so that a clone or a
release download is a complete, playable game — non-commercial, with
full attribution to Mark Mackey, exactly as the license requires.

Bundled files
-------------
  xquest.gfx    — all sprites (ship, enemies, objects, fonts, gates)
  xquest.enm    — binary enemy definitions
  xquest.fnt    — small in-game status-bar font
  xquest2.fnt   — large Comix menu font
  xquest.snd    — raw 8-bit 11025 Hz mono PCM sound effects
  startpic.pbm  — title-screen planar bitmap (startpic.raw is generated
                  from it at build time by tools/convert_pbm.py)

Not bundled (gitignored)
-------------------------
  *.json                 — this project's own decoded/human-readable
                            dumps from tools/decode_assets.py. Redundant
                            with the binary files above; the compiled
                            engine never reads them.
  config.json/.cfg,
  hiscores.json/.scr      — personal save state, not game content.

To refresh from a newer or different original distribution, run:

    scripts/fetch-assets.sh

That script copies the required files from an adjacent ../xquest/
directory (an original DOS source/binary distribution).

A separate, complete archival copy of the original XQuest distribution
(source, .exe, docs — everything) is attached to a dedicated GitHub
Release for preservation purposes; it is not part of any installable
build. See the repository's Releases page.
